From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stage C <stage-c@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:40:33 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: feed cached CGUs to synchronous codegen

The stage-C patch that runs codegen synchronously on wasm
(0001-wasm-run-compiler-and-codegen-on-calling-thread) replaced the
coordinator thread's message loop, but only for freshly compiled CGUs:
submit_codegened_module_to_llvm calls the synchronous path directly, while
the two cached-module submit functions still sent messages into the
coordinator channel that no thread drains.

On the second incremental compilation, unchanged CGUs are reused with
CguReuse::PostLto and submitted through submit_post_lto_module_to_llvm as
WorkItem::CopyPostLtoArtifacts. With no coordinator thread that message was
dropped, so the reused object files never reached the linker and Wild
reported undefined symbols for drop glue and generic alloc/core
instantiations. The first incremental run works because all CGUs are
compiled afresh, and -Ccodegen-units=1 hides the problem because there is
no cross-CGU reuse.

Handle the cached path in synchronous codegen as well: copy the cached
artifacts inline with execute_copy_from_cache_work_item, exactly as the
coordinator thread does for CopyPostLtoArtifacts, and push the resulting
module into CompiledModules. Pre-LTO reuse only exists for LTO builds, which
this codegen backend does not support, so fail loudly rather than dropping
it. The copy helper is a free function at the end of the file so that this
patch stays outside the hunks of 0001 and the build script's
reverse-check-based idempotence keeps working.

A second incremental compile of plugin (c) reproduced the failure before
this change (reused object plus fresh allocator object only; Wild reported
undefined drop_glue/RawVec/Iterator symbols). With the fix applied to the
combined-build rustc.wasm, stage-c/run.sh incremental passes for plugin (c)
and A.2 (e) on every cold and incremental run, and
difftest/incremental-check.sh passes for corpus smoke.rs. The measured
numbers and the output-size caveat are in stage-c/notes/incremental.md.
Changed by the contributors to the rust_wasm repository.
---
 compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/write.rs | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/write.rs b/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/write.rs
index dcc57ef..dba129e 100644
--- a/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/write.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/write.rs
@@ -2314,6 +2314,10 @@ pub(crate) fn submit_post_lto_module_to_llvm<B: WriteBackendMethods>(
     coordinator: &Coordinator<B>,
     module: CachedModuleCodegen,
 ) {
+    if let Some(sync) = &coordinator.sync {
+        copy_cached_sync_module(&mut sync.borrow_mut(), module);
+        return;
+    }
     let llvm_work_item = WorkItem::CopyPostLtoArtifacts(module);
     drop(coordinator.sender.send(Message::CodegenDone::<B> { llvm_work_item, cost: 0 }));
 }
@@ -2323,6 +2327,15 @@ pub(crate) fn submit_pre_lto_module_to_llvm<B: WriteBackendMethods>(
     coordinator: &Coordinator<B>,
     module: CachedModuleCodegen,
 ) {
+    // Pre-LTO reuse only exists for LTO builds, which this backend does not
+    // support. Fail loudly instead of leaving the cached module in the
+    // coordinator channel that synchronous codegen never drains.
+    if coordinator.sync.is_some() {
+        tcx.sess.dcx().fatal(
+            "synchronous wasm codegen does not support pre-LTO incremental reuse: \
+             LTO is not supported by this codegen backend",
+        );
+    }
     let filename = pre_lto_bitcode_filename(&module.name);
     let old_bitcode_path =
         in_old_incr_comp_dir_sess(tcx.incr_comp_session.unwrap(), &filename).unwrap();
@@ -2374,3 +2387,23 @@ fn msvc_imps_needed(tcx: TyCtxt<'_>) -> bool {
     // dynamic linking when linker plugin LTO is enabled.
     !tcx.sess.opts.cg.linker_plugin_lto.enabled()
 }
+
+/// Copy a CGU reused from the incremental cache into a synchronous
+/// [`SyncCodegen`]'s module list.
+///
+/// When codegen has a coordinator thread, `WorkItem::CopyPostLtoArtifacts`
+/// travels through that thread's queue. In synchronous mode there is no thread
+/// to drain the queue, so the copy happens inline instead; without it, reused
+/// object files never reach the linker.
+fn copy_cached_sync_module<B: WriteBackendMethods>(
+    sync: &mut SyncCodegen<B>,
+    module: CachedModuleCodegen,
+) {
+    let compiled = execute_copy_from_cache_work_item(
+        &sync.cgcx,
+        &sync.prof,
+        sync.shared_emitter.clone(),
+        module,
+    );
+    sync.compiled_modules.push(compiled);
+}
